---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PageSummary from '../../components/PageSummary.astro';
import NextSteps from '../../components/NextSteps.astro';

const page = { dateModified: '2026-11-27' };
const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", url: "https://arthavi.com/" },
  { name: "Blog", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/" },
  { name: "Track Zerodha and Groww together", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/track-zerodha-groww-portfolio-together/" }
];
const faqs = [
  { q: "Can I use Zerodha and Groww together?", a: "Yes. SEBI (Securities and Exchange Board of India) rules allow you to open demat and trading accounts with more than one broker under the same PAN. Many investors use Zerodha for stocks and Groww for mutual fund SIPs." },
  { q: "Can I have two Demat accounts in India?", a: "Yes. You can have multiple demat accounts linked to the same PAN across brokers like Zerodha, Groww and Angel One. Each demat account has its own account number (BO ID)." },
  { q: "How can I view my Zerodha and Groww portfolio together?", a: "Use a tracker that imports statements instead of logging in to your brokers. In Arthavi you upload your CAS (Consolidated Account Statement) for mutual funds and the holdings or tradebook file from Zerodha Console and Groww for stocks, and see one combined dashboard with XIRR. No broker login is needed." },
  { q: "Do I need to give Arthavi my Zerodha or Groww password?", a: "No. Arthavi never asks for broker passwords, OTPs or email access. It works only from the files you download and upload yourself." },
  { q: "Does Arthavi update automatically when I buy more shares?", a: "Prices and NAVs update automatically, but new transactions come in when you upload a fresh CAS or tradebook file, or add the trade by hand." },
];

const seo = {
  title: "Can I Use Zerodha and Groww Together? How to Track Both (2026) | Arthavi",
  description: "Yes, you can use Zerodha and Groww together! Learn SEBI rules, why investors use both brokers, and how to track your combined portfolio in one private dashboard.",
};
---
<Layout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  keywords="can i use zerodha and groww together, track zerodha and groww together, can i have zerodha and groww demat account, zerodha groww portfolio consolidation, best app to track stocks and mutual funds india"
  schema={JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "headline": "Can You Use Zerodha and Groww Together? How to Track Both in One Place",
        "image": "https://arthavi.com/images/og-image.png",
        "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Arthavi" },
        "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Arthavi", "logo": { "@type": "ImageObject", "url": "https://arthavi.com/images/logo.png" } },
        "datePublished": "2026-02-16",
        "dateModified": "2026-11-27",
        "description": "Learn if you can use Zerodha and Groww together and how to consolidate both portfolios into one dashboard securely."
      },
      {
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": faqs.map((f) => ({ "@type": "Question", "name": f.q, "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": f.a } }))
      }
    ]
  })}
  breadcrumb={{ items: crumbs }}
  dateModified={page.dateModified}
>

    <main class="container" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem);">
        <article class="prose fade-in" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
            <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
            <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Can You Use Zerodha and Groww Together? (How to Track Both in One Place)</h1>

            <PageSummary
              dateModified={page.dateModified}
              answer="<strong>Yes, you can use Zerodha and Groww together.</strong> SEBI rules let you hold demat accounts with several brokers under one PAN. To see both in one place without sharing passwords, use <strong>Arthavi</strong>, a free portfolio tracker: upload your CAS (Consolidated Account Statement) for mutual funds and the <a href='/stock-tradebook-import/'>holdings or tradebook file</a> from each broker for stocks. You get one combined net worth and XIRR, and no broker login is ever needed."
              terms={['SEBI', 'PAN', 'CAS', 'CAMS', 'XIRR', 'ISIN', 'SIP', 'SMS']}
            />

            <p style="font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">
                The classic Indian investor dilemma: You perform your stock trading on <strong><a href="/arthavi-vs-zerodha/">Zerodha Kite</a></strong>
                because of its clean UI, but you started your SIPs on <strong><a href="/arthavi-vs-groww/">Groww</a></strong> because it was easy to set
                up.
            </p>

            <p>Now, you have a fragmented net worth. You have to open two apps, check two different totals, and mentally
                add them up to know how rich (or poor) you are today.</p>

            <div
                style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2rem; background: var(--bg-surface); border-radius: 12px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05);">
                <h2 style="margin-top: 0;">Why not just move everything to one app?</h2>
                <p>Moving your entire portfolio is a hassle. It involves:</p>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 0;">
                    <li>Closing a Demat account (painful paperwork).</li>
                    <li>Stopping and restarting SIPs (losing track of vintage).</li>
                    <li>Paying capital gains tax if you sell and rebuy.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">It's smarter to keep your brokers as they are and use a <strong>unified
                        layer</strong> on top.</p>
            </div>

            <h2>Why are many "unified" apps risky?</h2>
            <p>Many popular apps (we won't name them) offer to "sync" your Zerodha and Groww accounts. They do this by
                asking for:</p>
            <ol>
                <li>Your broker username/password (Huge security risk!).</li>
                <li>Your email access to read contract notes (Privacy risk!).</li>
                <li>Your SMS permissions to read transaction alerts.</li>
            </ol>
            <p><strong>This is a bad trade.</strong> You are giving away the keys to your financial kingdom just to see
                a pie chart.</p>

            <div class="glass-panel" style="margin: 3rem 0; padding: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--primary-glow);">
                <h2 style="margin-top: 0; color: var(--primary-glow);">How does Arthavi track Zerodha and Groww safely?</h2>
                <p>Arthavi allows you to track Zerodha (Stocks) and Groww (Mutual Funds) together <strong>without
                        linking your accounts</strong>.</p>

                <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">How It Works:</h3>

                <h4 style="color: var(--text-head); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">For Groww (Mutual
                    Funds):</h4>
                <p>Every mutual fund you buy on Groww is recorded by the fund's registrar, CAMS or KFintech. Download
                    your <strong>Consolidated Account Statement (CAS)</strong> from <a href="https://www.camsonline.com/Investors/Statements/Consolidated-Account-Statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CAMS</a>
                    or <a href="https://mfs.kfintech.com/investor/General/ConsolidatedAccountStatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">KFintech</a> and upload it to Arthavi. It lists every folio across all fund houses,
                    including funds bought on Zerodha Coin.</p>

                <h4 style="color: var(--text-head); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; margin-top: 1.5rem;">For Zerodha (Stocks):
                </h4>
                <p>Export your holdings or tradebook from Zerodha Console as a CSV or Excel file and upload it in Arthavi
                    (see <a href="/stock-tradebook-import/">stock tradebook import</a>). Arthavi matches each ISIN to its NSE / BSE
                    listing and keeps prices up to date. Groww stock holdings work the same way.</p>

                <div style="margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center;">
                    <a href="https://app.arthavi.com/register" class="btn btn-primary">Consolidate My Portfolio Free</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h2>Benefits of a Consolidated View</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>True Net Worth:</strong> See the sum of Stocks + Mutual Funds + Cash in one number.</li>
                <li><strong>Asset Allocation:</strong> Realize that you are actually 80% exposed to equity when you
                    thought you were balanced.</li>
                <li><strong>Tax view:</strong> One <a href="/capital-gains-tax-report/">capital gains report</a> across both brokers, plus every <a href="/sip-tracker/">SIP</a> in one list.</li>
                <li><strong>Family view:</strong> Add your spouse's or parents' Zerodha and Groww accounts as separate <a href="/family-portfolio-tracker/">family profiles</a>.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>How do you set it up, step by step?</h2>
            <ol>
                <li><strong>Sign up:</strong> Create a <a href="https://app.arthavi.com/register">free Arthavi account</a>.</li>
                <li><strong>Import Mutual Funds:</strong> Use the "Import Investments" feature (See our <a
                        href="/blog/how-to-download-analyze-cams-cas-statement/">guide on downloading your investment statement</a>).</li>
                <li><strong>Import Stocks:</strong> Go to Zerodha Console > Portfolio > Holdings > Download CSV (or download your tradebook). Upload
                    this to Arthavi. Repeat for Groww.</li>
                <li><strong>Done!</strong> Your unified dashboard is ready.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>What Arthavi does not do</h2>
            <p>Arthavi does not place trades and does not connect to Zerodha or Groww directly, so new trades appear only after you upload a fresh file or add them by hand.</p>

            <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
            {faqs.map((f) => (
              <details class="glass-panel" style="padding: 1rem 1.25rem; border-radius: 12px; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
                <summary style="cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-head);">{f.q}</summary>
                <p style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0;">{f.a}</p>
              </details>
            ))}

            <NextSteps heading="See Zerodha and Groww in one dashboard" cta="Consolidate my portfolio free" sources />

        </article>
    </main>

</Layout>
